From: sjcsf <346224915+llsf2020@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 09:05:19 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 02/15] FreeChat: admin-only auto-delete, burn after reading,
 no deleted placeholders

- Room auto-delete can only be changed by room admins (power level 100 or
  creators); others see why
- Settings: default burn-after-read delay for my messages; room details:
  per-chat override or follow the default. Stored as global
  com.freechat.disappearing account data {read_ttl, rooms}, because the
  Rust SDK cannot write room account data
- Every deleted message disappears without a placeholder, like Telegram;
  deleted thread roots stay. Two upstream TimelinePresenter tests adapted
- Shared duration labels in libraries/matrixui
